# Adding a new MF remote

Do **not** hand-copy shop/cart vite configs, shell remotes, router routes, sider links, or Tailwind `@source` lines.

## One command

```bash
bun run create-remote --name <kebab-name> --port <port>
# optional: --title "Orders" --blurb "Order list remote"
```

Example:

```bash
bun run create-remote --name orders --port 5103
```

## What that updates

| Piece | Where | Manual? |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| Registry | `packages/mf-config/remotes.json` | script |
| App scaffold | `apps/<name>/` (thin vite + App) | script |
| Shell MF remotes | `createShellViteConfig` reads JSON | auto |
| Routes / sider / home | shell reads `REMOTES` | auto |
| `bun run dev` | `scripts/dev-all.mjs` reads JSON | auto |
| Tailwind scan | `apps/*/src` glob | auto |

## After create

1. Implement UI in `apps/<name>/src/App.tsx` (expose stays `./App`).
2. `bun run dev` — shell + all remotes.

## Shared config (do not duplicate)

- Remote Vite: `@react-mfe/mf-config/vite` → `createRemoteViteConfig`
- Shell Vite: `createShellViteConfig`
- Shared singletons / ports / titles: `packages/mf-config/remotes.json`

## Removing a remote

```bash
bun run delete-remote --name promotions
# registry only (keep apps/<name>):
bun run delete-remote --name promotions --keep-files
# orphan folder after a failed delete (Vite lock):
bun run delete-remote --name cart --force
```

Removes `remotes.json` entry and (by default) `apps/<name>/`. Stop `bun run dev` first on Windows — Vite locks the folder (`EACCES` / `EBUSY`). Shell + `bun run dev` pick registry changes up automatically.

